


HOSTNAME(1)         UNIX Programmer's Manual          HOSTNAME(1)



NAME
     hostname - set or print name of current host system

SYNOPSIS
     hostname [ nameofhost ]

DESCRIPTION
     The _h_o_s_t_n_a_m_e command prints the name of the current host, as
     given before the ``login'' prompt.  The super-user can set
     the hostname by giving an argument; this is usually done in
     the startup script /etc/rc.local.

SEE ALSO
     gethostname(2), sethostname(2)









































